<BaseLayout title="Buy Better Finds Standards | Product Research & Buy Better Score" description="Learn how Buy Better Finds researches, evaluates, compares, and scores products using its independent Buy Better Score editorial framework.">
  <article class="article">
    <div class="eyebrow">Buy Better Finds Standards</div>
    <h1>How Buy Better Finds Evaluates Products</h1>
    <p class="lead">Buy Better Finds is an independent product research and evaluation publication. Our editorial framework explains how we assess product information, compare meaningful differences, identify tradeoffs, and develop recommendations for shoppers.</p>

    <h2>Our evaluation process</h2>
    <h3>01 — Research</h3>
    <p>We review available product information, including manufacturer specifications, listed features, intended uses, compatibility details, dimensions, materials, care or maintenance needs, and other information that may affect a purchasing decision.</p>

    <h3>02 — Compare</h3>
    <p>When relevant alternatives are available, we compare practical differences such as intended use, features, convenience, size, compatibility, value, and limitations. A longer feature list does not automatically make a product the better choice.</p>

    <h3>03 — Evaluate</h3>
    <p>We consider how well the available product information supports the needs of its intended shopper. We explain the product's strengths, meaningful limitations, and the situations in which another option may be a better fit.</p>

    <h3>04 — Recommend</h3>
    <p>Our recommendations are editorial judgments based on the evaluation. We aim to explain who may benefit from a product, what to consider before buying, and what tradeoffs should be understood.</p>

    <h2>How the Buy Better Score works</h2>
    <p>The Buy Better Score is our own editorial assessment on a 10-point scale. It is designed to make our evaluations easier to understand and compare. We consider five practical areas:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Use-case fit:</strong> how well the product appears suited to the needs and situations it is intended to serve.</li>
      <li><strong>Useful features:</strong> whether the listed features meaningfully support the product's intended purpose.</li>
      <li><strong>Practicality:</strong> considerations such as convenience, setup, size, compatibility, maintenance, and everyday usability based on available information.</li>
      <li><strong>Value:</strong> what the product offers in relation to its price positioning and relevant alternatives.</li>
      <li><strong>Tradeoffs:</strong> limitations, compromises, compatibility concerns, recurring costs, or reasons a shopper may prefer another option.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>The Buy Better Score reflects our editorial judgment; it is not a retailer rating, customer-review average, laboratory result, or guarantee of performance. Scores are not assigned by a retailer or advertiser, and affiliate compensation does not determine a product's score.</p>

    <h2>Research-based evaluations and hands-on reviews</h2>
    <p>Most Buy Better Finds product evaluations are research-based. They use available product specifications, manufacturer information, feature descriptions, and other decision-relevant information. A research-based evaluation should not be interpreted as a claim that we purchased, handled, or personally tested the product.</p>
    <p>We identify hands-on testing only when a product has actually been received and used by a reviewer. When hands-on testing takes place, the relevant review will describe the testing status and distinguish firsthand observations from information supplied by the manufacturer or other sources.</p>

    <h2>Affiliate links and editorial independence</h2>
    <p>Some links on this site are affiliate links. We may earn a commission when a qualifying purchase is made. Affiliate compensation does not determine our scores, editorial conclusions, or recommendations. A product is not given a higher score because it offers a commission.</p>
    <p><strong>As an Amazon Associate I earn from qualifying purchases.</strong></p>

    <h2>Prices, availability, and product information</h2>
    <p>Retail prices, promotions, stock, shipping, warranties, specifications, and return policies can change. Confirm current details with the retailer or manufacturer before purchasing. Where we provide price context, it should be understood in light of the date and source shown on the relevant page.</p>

    <h2>Images and sourcing</h2>
    <p>We use manufacturer media resources, authorized press materials, original photography, and other imagery where appropriate usage rights are established. Manufacturer or retailer imagery is not represented as original Buy Better Finds photography.</p>

    <h2>Review updates</h2>
    <p>Product pages may be revisited when product versions, meaningful alternatives, availability, or other decision-relevant information changes. Any stated hands-on testing status applies only to the product and review where it is disclosed.</p>

